."y\b<b>Curtis</b>: Vi aspettiamo nella città di Odeya per fornirvi il vostro pokémon Starter. Buona fortuna a tutti!"Maschio"Femmina"Si"NoIu;␀E[[";\bThese doors are examples of good, solid door events."~\bWhen the player goes outside, be sure to transfer the player onto the door rather than next to it. It looks better that way.[@"\bWhen the player goes outside, be sure to transfer the player onto the door rather than next to it.  It looks better that way.;[";\bThese doors are examples of good, solid door events."~\bWhen the player goes outside, be sure to transfer the player onto the door rather than next to it. It looks better that way.Iu;␀K"[[m"Choose a topic.";Do you want to record your voice for the Trainer Card?"(Thank you. Check your Trainer Card."=You can record your voice later if you change your mind."}Choose a destination.\ch[1,-1,Game Corner,Trainer area,Shadow Pokémon area,Bridges map,Water map, Harbour,Cycle Road,Cancel]"�The $Trainer global variable contains valuable information on the player, including their trainer type, ID, name, party Pokémon, money, and so on."@Refer to PokeBattle_Trainer for details on Trainer objects."]The Map Connector (also known as the Visual Editor) allows you to connect maps together."VIn the Debug menu (F9 or in the pause menu), choose the "Map Connections" option."�Once there, choose a map to display by pressing the S key. Select it and press the E key to edit its encounters, or double-click it to edit its metadata."�Add additional maps to the canvas by pressing the A key, and drag them around to connect them. Maps only connect if just their edges touch."}Every tile in a tileset has a terrain tag, which is a number. This number is used to give certain tiles special effects."�For example, ledge tiles have terrain tag 1, which means the player jumps over them. Ledge tiles also have a single passable direction (set separately)."qGrass tiles (in which you can have wild encounters) have terrain tag 2. Water tiles have terrain tag 6 or 7."�Terrain tag 0 means the tile has no special effect. See the wiki for more information and a complete list of all terrain tags and their effects."uTo set a tileset's terrain tags, open the Debug menu (F9 or from the pause menu) and choose "Edit Terrain Tags"."h\rThe "Choices" event command cannot allow more than 4 choices. This is what you should do instead."XPlease choose one.\ch[1,-1, Choice 1,Choice 2,Choice 3, Choice 4,Choice 5,Choice 6]"The choice was cancelled."Choice 1 was chosen."Choice 2 was chosen."Choice 3 was chosen."Choice 4 was chosen."Choice 5 was chosen."Choice 6 was chosen."PPlease choose one. This choice can't be canceled.\ch[1,0,Choice 1,Choice 2]"TMultiple choice commands like these are enabled using the \\ch message command."�The bracketed area after \\ch consists of the Variable to store the choice, a default choice in case the player cancels, and then a number of choices."@If the default choice is set to 0, the player can't cancel."\The $DEBUG flag was set. This flag is set automatically during playtesting within RMXP."{Debug mode allows you to access the Debug menu (F9 or in the pause menu), and to modify Pokémon in your party/the PC."xYou can also use hidden moves anytime, and hold CTRL to skip any battles and decide the outcome of Trainer battles.":Obtained all badges for the first and second regions."VTo add a badge, use $Trainer.badges[X]=true where X is a number from 0 through 7.">In Debug mode, you can set your badges in the Debug menu."/Press F8 to take a screenshot of the game."JThe screenshot will be put in the folder where the save file is kept."Choose a text option."V\bThis is the text of a male character. \rThis is the text of a female character."y\pgThis text is the colour of the player's gender. \pogThis text is the colour of the opposite gender to the player."�\c[0]Default text, \c[1]blue text, \c[2]red text, \c[3] green text, \c[4]cyan text, \c[5]magenta text, \c[6] yellow t